.TH SIMRV-PARITY 1 "November 2026" "SimRV 3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
simrv-parity \- compare SimRV execution with hardware-model targets
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B simrv-parity
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ target ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B simrv-parity
evaluates SimRV against a registered RTL or hardware-model target. Targets may
be built in or loaded from an external parity plugin.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-list-targets
List registered and discovered targets.
.TP
.B \-\-plugin \fILIBRARY\fR
Load an external parity target adapter.
.TP
.B \-\-simrv \fIPATH\fR
Select the simulator executable.
.TP
.B \-\-target-dir \fIPATH\fR
Select a target checkout; \fBRVCOMP_DIR\fR and \fBCFU_PG_DIR\fR are also
recognized.
.TP
.B \-\-target-bin \fIPATH\fR
Select a prebuilt Verilator simulator executable.
.TP
.B \-\-config \fIPATH\fR
Use a custom SimRV platform or CPU configuration.
.TP
.B \-\-trace-dir \fIPATH\fR, \-\-work-dir \fIPATH\fR
Choose directories for traces and intermediate build artifacts.
.TP
.B \-\-out \fIPATH\fR
Write the evaluation summary as JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-tune, \-\-quick, \-\-apply
Tune configuration parameters, use a coarse search, or apply the selected
parameters to the configuration file.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display help and exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR simrv (1),
.BR simrv-tune (1)
